    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`, on the owner response.\n\nThree coordinated changes, each in its proper layer:\n\n1. **API contract** \u2014 `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: added a read-only `contactPreference` enum property (`EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived read-only fields. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **Domain rule** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../util/ContactPreference.java` (new): a pure enum with `static of(Owner)` that returns `EMAIL` when the email is present (non-null, non-blank) and `PHONE` otherwise, `null` for a null owner. This mirrors the existing `MembershipLevel` precedent and keeps the rule as a single-responsibility, testable function independent of the DTO layer.\n\n3. **Mapping** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`: added a `contactPreference` `@Mapping` expression and a small `default` helper that delegates to `ContactPreference.of(...)` and converts the domain enum to the generated `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` by name. This automatically covers every owner-emitting endpoint (get, list, created, updated) since they all go through the mapper.\n\nThe two new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
